`startChangeDetection(options)` is fire-and-forget with no error handler. Any rejection thrown inside — from `presets.apply`, `indexGenerator.getIndex()`, or `warmupRequest` — will become an unhandled promise rejection and be silently swallowed in most environments. Add at minimum a `.catch()` to log the failure:

```ts
startChangeDetection(options).catch((e) =>
  logger.error('Change detection failed to initialise', e)
);
```

Commented-out debug log should be removed before merge:
```ts
// logger.info(`Story ${entry.id} absolute path: ${absolutePath}`);
```

`getChangedFiles()` begins with `const repoRoot = await this.getRepoRoot()` internally. Because both `getChangedFiles()` and `getRepoRoot()` are kicked off in the same `Promise.all`, neither has had a chance to populate `this.repoRoot` before the other reads the cache — so two concurrent `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` processes can be spawned. The simplest fix is to call `getRepoRoot()` once before the `Promise.all` and pass it through, or to cache the in-flight promise rather than the resolved value:
```ts
const repoRoot = await gitDiffProvider.getRepoRoot();
const [changes, storyIndexGenerator] = await Promise.all([
  gitDiffProvider.getChangedFiles(),
  this.options.storyIndexGeneratorPromise,
]);
```
